; Repo-level npm config (safe to commit — contains no secrets).
; The workspace plugins (zest-astro, zest-eleventy) declare astro / eleventy as
; peerDependencies with no devDependency fallback. With npm's default peer
; auto-install, CI would expect those peers pinned in package-lock.json while
; local installs (which honor a global legacy-peer-deps) omit them — desyncing
; the lockfile and breaking `npm ci`. Pin the behavior here so local and CI
; agree. This only affects installs run *inside* this repo, never consumers.
legacy-peer-deps=true